! mcp_bootstrap_p109.strap -- printed page 109:
! "********PROGRAM STATUS TABLE**********".
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.116, header READ AND NOT ASSUMED:
! the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP  CARD ID
! DA000001  DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 109".  The page
! number was rendered on its own at 600 dpi and reads 109 in clean
! digits; the +7 offset is not assumed here, it is confirmed.
!
! TEN LINES, AND THAT IS COUNTED, NOT ESTIMATED.  The card-serial
! column prints DA000001 through DA000010, ten rows, and the printed
! line numbers run 1 to 10 with no gap.  Below line 10 the page is
! blank to the bottom rule.  (The serial PREFIX is read "DA" and is
! NOT claimed with confidence -- the pair sits in this drum's O/C/D
! failure class and nothing depends on it.  It is worth recording
! only because p.103 prints CA and p.104 prints CB, so the prefix is
! a per-punched-deck serial and this page starts a new one again.)
!
! >>> WHAT THE PAGE IS. <<<  Four heading cards, an SLC and a CNOP
! that realign the location counter, ONE storage card -- a two-word
! zeroed reservation named S PROG S -- and three SYN cards that name
! bits inside it.  That is the whole page.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ADDRESS CHAIN CLOSES ON BOTH SIDES, AND BOTH ENDS WERE READ
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THIS PAGE DISCHARGES printed p.104's STANDING REQUEST. <<<
! decks/mcp_bootstrap_p104.strap, SUBSTITUTIONS note (1), asks that
! when pp.100-103 land, "the counter they leave behind must be
! compared BY HAND against this page's printed 215020.71".  Done,
! and it agrees:
!
!   printed p.103 line 56 is "S TERMI VF,ZFINIS" at 215020.40.
!   A VF is TWENTY-FIVE BITS (decks/mcp_bootstrap_p48.strap's bit
!   chain is the witness), and 0o40 + 25 = 57 = 0o71.
!   So the counter p.103 leaves behind is 215020.71.
!
!   printed p.104 line 6 is "SLC,$" and prints 215020.71.
!   printed p.109 line 5 is "SLC,$" and prints 215020.71.
!
! Two pages print the arriving counter and the page before them
! computes it.  Three independent readings, one value.
!
! THE FAR SIDE CLOSES TOO.  Line 7's DRZ(BU,64),2 is two words at
! 215021.00, so the counter leaves this page at 215023.00 --
! and printed p.110 line 5 ("SLC,$", the INTERRUPT TABLE) PRINTS
! 215023.00.  Read off PDF p.117 for this deck; not assumed.
!
! >>> pp.105-108 CONSUME NO STORAGE, AND THE TWO SLCs SAY SO. <<<
! The counter printed by p.104's SLC and the counter printed by
! p.109's SLC are the same bit, so nothing between them moved it.
! Those four pages are not transcribed and this deck does not claim
! to know what they contain -- only that whatever it is, it spends
! no storage.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE CNOP EMITS NOTHING, AND THE PAGE PRINTS THAT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 6's CNOP prints an EMPTY LOCATION and an EMPTY BINARY OUTPUT
! column -- the only row on the page with a statement and no
! location.  That is not a dropout: the counter arrives at
! 215020.71, a CNOP first rounds up to the next HALF word, and
! 0o71 is 57 so seven zero bits reach 215021.00, which is ALREADY a
! full-word address.  No NOP is needed, so none is compiled and
! there is nothing to print.  (strap_asm does the same thing: its
! gap filler computes pad = (-gap_start) % HALF = 7, lays the seven
! zero bits, and finds no half word left to fill.  See the comment
! above "pad = (-gap_start) % HALF" in strap/strap_asm.py.)
! Compare printed p.103 line 48, whose CNOP arrives at a half-word
! boundary and DOES print "215013.40 * 000000.30 00".
!
! >>> THE FLAG-COLUMN ASTERISK IS ABSENT HERE, AND THAT WAS
! MEASURED. <<<  printed p.104 line 6 and printed p.110 line 5 are
! the same "SLC,$" card and BOTH print a "*" in the one-character
! column between LOCATION and BINARY OUTPUT.  printed p.109 line 5
! does NOT.  Checked by rendering the identical window -- 1800 dpi,
! x=6900 y=3330 W=1900 -- on PDF p.117 and PDF p.116 and montaging
! the two: p.110's asterisk is in frame and p.109's row is blank
! across the same column.  Recorded, not explained.  Nothing in
! this deck depends on it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE FOUR HEADING CARDS (lines 1-4) ARE NOT TRANSCRIBED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! They carry no LOCATION and no BINARY OUTPUT and print as raw card
! images from column 2 on, which is printed p.103's pair of tells.
! They read:
!   1  **********************************************************
!   2       ********PROGRAM STATUS TABLE**********
!   3  **********************************************************
!   4  (blank after the column-2 dash)
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! NO EXTERNAL SYMBOLS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every operand on this page is a literal -- "2", ".25", ".32",
! ".61".  Nothing on the page references a name defined elsewhere,
! so there are no SYN stand-ins to declare and that section of the
! house format is legitimately empty.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE NAMES
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The NAME column is eight characters and prints blanks inside the
! name, exactly as printed p.103's "S COM SZ" does.  Read at 1800
! dpi:
!
!   line  7  "S PROG S"  -> SPROGS
!   line  8  "S A S"     -> SAS
!   line  9  "S Q K"     -> SQK     (a clean Q: the tail is printed)
!   line 10  "S SIO"     -> SSIO
!
! THE COMMENT COLUMN IS AN ORACLE FOR PART OF TWO OF THEM, AND NO
! MORE THAN THAT.  Line 7's comment is "-PROGRAM STATUS TABLE",
! which spells PROG for me; line 8's is "-AUTO STACK STATUS
! INDICATOR", which spells the A.  Neither comment spells the
! trailing S of a name -- those are read off the glyph at 1800 dpi,
! where an S is unambiguous on this drum, and the comment is not
! claimed as evidence for them.  Line 9 carries NO comment at all.
!
! >>> SSIO's LAST GLYPH, SETTLED BY THE ASYMMETRY RULE AND NOT BY
! RESEMBLANCE. <<<  It is a round glyph, so O, C, D and 0 are all
! on the table.  D is out at once: D prints a straight vertical
! LEFT stem and squared corners and this glyph's left side is a
! bowl.  For O against C the page supplies its own controls, and
! all three were cropped at 1800 dpi at identical size and
! montaged beside the glyph:
!
!   the O of "MODE" in line 10's own comment          (English: O)
!   the C of "INDICATOR" in line 10's own comment     (English: C)
!   the O of "INDICATOR" in line 10's own comment     (English: O)
!
! The known C has its mid-right side CLEANLY ABSENT with both
! terminals curling inward and a blob on the lower terminal.  The
! glyph in question has ink on the mid-right and the lower right --
! a broken ring, not an open arc -- which is how this drum's O
! prints in the very same comment ("MODE"'s O is broken the same
! way).  The rule in docs/transcription_workflow.md runs one way:
! DROPOUT CAN OPEN A CLOSED GLYPH BUT NEVER CLOSES AN OPEN ONE.  A
! ring with ink on its right side therefore cannot be a damaged C,
! because that would require ink to have been ADDED.  So the
! reading is O.
!
! >>> AND IT RESTS ON INK ALONE, WHICH IS SAID OUT LOUD. <<<  A
! grep over every deck and every test in the repository finds NO
! other page that mentions SPROGS, SAS, SQK or SSIO.  None of the
! four is referenced anywhere, so tests/check_symbol_spellings.py
! has nothing to cross-check them against and a misspelling here
! would assemble perfectly and pass every check in this repository.
! The weakest of the four is SSIO, whose comment ("-SUPPRESSED MODE
! STATUS INDICATOR") does not spell its name out the way lines 7
! and 8 do.  printed p.104 establishes that MCP writes "S" for its
! suppress-wait pseudo-op variants (D RD / D RD S), which makes
! "suppressed I/O" a plausible expansion of S + SIO -- that is
! SUGGESTIVE ONLY and is not what the reading rests on.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT IS CHECKED AND WHAT IS NOT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FOUR !SYM LINES AND ZERO !CHECK LINES, and that is correct.
!
! * The three SYN cards deposit no storage word.  printed p.99's
!   convention, restated by printed p.104: a SYN is checked in
!   !SYM and must NOT be faked into a !CHECK.
! * Line 7 is a DRZ, and the "000002.00" it prints in the BINARY
!   OUTPUT column is the reservation's SIZE, not its contents --
!   0o2 is two, and the two words it reserves are zeros.  printed
!   p.84 gives its DRZ rows no !CHECK for the same reason.  0o2 = 2
!   IS still read: it is the count in the statement, and the count
!   is what puts printed p.110's SLC at 215023.00.
!
! WHICH OF THE FOUR SYMBOLS ARE LOAD-BEARING:
! * SAS, SQK and SSIO are the real independent checks.  Their
!   values resolve from the DECIMAL bit offsets .25, .32 and .61
!   written on the cards -- 25 = 0o31, 32 = 0o40, 61 = 0o75 --
!   against the printed 000000.31+, 000000.40+ and 000000.75+, and
!   they do not depend on the origin at all.
! * SPROGS does NOT check the origin.  The hard SLC below asserts
!   it.  What SPROGS checks is the CNOP's alignment: that .71
!   rounds to 215021.00 and not past it.
!
! NOT CHECKED: the SYN rows' printed DATA DESCRIPTIONS
! ("BU,01 ,10", "BU,22 ,10", "BU,01 ,10").  listing_oracle has no
! renderer for them, exactly as printed p.103 records.  They are
! transcribed into the listing block below and are NOT
! independently verified -- a SYN(BU,18) written as SYN(BU,1) would
! pass everything here.  0o22 = 18 and 0o10 = 8 is the arithmetic
! that reads them.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SUBSTITUTIONS AND OMISSIONS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) LINE 5'S CARD IS "SLC,$" AND THIS DECK WRITES
!     "SLC, (8)215020.71", for printed p.104's reason: in an
!     isolated deck "$" is zero, not 0o215020.71, so transcribing
!     the card verbatim would record a different fact than the page
!     prints.  strap_asm DOES accept a bare "SLC, $" -- this is a
!     deliberate substitution, not an assembler limitation, and the
!     printed card is recorded verbatim in the listing block.
!     The bit offset is written .71 EXACTLY AS PRINTED, because
!     inside an (8) literal BOTH parts are base 8.
!     AND IT COSTS THE SAME CHECK IT COST p.104: a hard SLC cannot
!     disagree with an arriving counter, it overrides it silently.
!     Here the disagreement is checked by hand instead, above, in
!     three readings that agree -- but if pp.105-108 are ever
!     transcribed and merged, this line should become a bare
!     "SLC,$" so the join becomes self-checking.
! (2) The four heading cards are not transcribed (see above).
! (3) Line 7's statement prints "DRZ(BU,64),  2" with the count
!     written BARE and right-shifted in the operand field.  This
!     deck writes "DRZ(BU,64), 2".  strap_asm's dr_count takes a
!     bare or a parenthesised count (strap/strap_asm.py's DR/DRZ
!     note cites printed p.24 line 52's bare "DRZ(BU),100"), so
!     this is spacing only, not a substitution of form.
! * NO OTHER SUBSTITUTIONS AND NO OMISSIONS AMONG THE CARDS THAT
!   COMPILE.  All six are below.

        SLC, (8)215020.71            ! line 5 -- printed card is "SLC,$"
        CNOP                         ! line 6 -- prints no location and
                                     !           no binary; see above

! ---- THE PROGRAM STATUS TABLE ------------------------------------
SPROGS  DRZ(BU,64), 2                ! line 7 -PROGRAM STATUS TABLE

! ---- BITS NAMED INSIDE IT, RELATIVE TO A ZERO BASE ---------------
! The bit offsets are BARE DECIMAL literals, so they are decimal and
! print octal: 25 -> 31, 32 -> 40, 61 -> 75.
SAS     SYN(BU,1), .25               ! line  8 -AUTO STACK STATUS
                                     !          INDICATOR
SQK     SYN(BU,18), .32              ! line  9 (no comment printed)
SSIO    SYN(BU,1), .61               ! line 10 -SUPPRESSED MODE STATUS
                                     !          INDICATOR

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING -- the six cards that are not comments.
! LOCATION, then BINARY OUTPUT with its data description, then NAME
! and STATEMENT, then the comment.  A row whose location ends in
! "+" is a SYN and the column prints its RESOLVED VALUE, not the
! counter.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   line  5  215020.71                                 SLC,$
!            (no "*" in the flag column -- see above)
!   line  6  (no location, no binary)                  CNOP
!   line  7  215021.00   000002.00                     S PROG S DRZ(BU,64),  2
!                                                        -PROGRAM STATUS TABLE
!   line  8  000000.31+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10       S A S    SYN(BU,1),.25
!                                                        -AUTO STACK STATUS INDICATOR
!   line  9  000000.40+  +00000000     BU,22 ,10       S Q K    SYN(BU,18),.32
!   line 10  000000.75+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10       S SIO    SYN(BU,1),.61
!                                                        -SUPPRESSED MODE STATUS INDICATOR
!
! Line 7's "000002.00" is the reservation's SIZE; see above.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! NO ASSEMBLER LIMITATION WAS HIT ON THIS PAGE.
! Every card that compiles is written in its printed form except
! the SLC, and that one substitution is documentary (note (1)).
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

! ---- CHECKS, read by tests/verify_mcp_page.py 109 ------------------
!SYM   SPROGS   215021.00
!SYM   SAS      000000.31
!SYM   SQK      000000.40
!SYM   SSIO     000000.75
